dcc-proxy (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Port the control center plugin to the V25 QML plugin ABI (Qt 6.8, DTK 6):
    install as plugins_v1.1/dccproxy with the qml/Dccproxy.qml metadata object
    and the eleven-page QML page tree (overview, proxies, profiles,
    connections, rules, providers, logs, override, tools, settings, tun).
  * Expose the whole plugin as a QML data object (dccData) from C++; the plugin
    no longer links QtWidgets and the widget page and preview binary are gone.
  * Manage the bundled core through the systemd user unit
    dde-mihomo-daemon.service (status/start/stop/enable from the plugin), while
    the daemon keeps running after the control center closes.
  * Build with Qt 6 / DTK 6 and dde-control-center 6.1 development files; drop
    every Qt 5 and DTK 5 build and runtime dependency.
  * Keep the bundled official Mihomo core, its root:root 4755 authorization and
    the offline geodata set; keep the login-autostart switch user controlled.
  * Draw the module and page icons as theme-aware DCI files (light and dark
    palettes) and restyle every page with the control center's own building
    blocks (section titles, group cards, aligned editor rows, table headers,
    empty states, palette-only colors).
  * Download subscriptions with a Mihomo-compatible User-Agent
    (mihomo/1.19.16, falling back to Mozilla/5.0 once on 403/404): many
    subscription panels answer browser user agents with 404 or HTML.
  * Poll only the data the visible page needs: the module reports the control
    center's active page, runtime models are rebuilt only when the displayed
    values change, and the log stream and connection list run only while their
    page is on screen (an idle control center used to burn a full core).
  * Update the smoke tests, Debian packaging and documentation for the V25
    layout (build/lib/plugins_v1.1/dccproxy).

 -- DCC Proxy maintainers <Mars-cb@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:30:00 +0800

